1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
TO MAMA. SEVENTY-ONE AND STILL COOKING.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,900
SORRY. IT'S THE SOAP THING.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,100
JADA. WE TALKED ABOUT THIS.

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,800
TALKED ABOUT WHAT?

5
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,700
YOU'RE PUTTING ME IN A HOME?

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,000
MAMA. WE WERE GONNA WAIT TILL AFTER CAKE.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,600
ON MY BIRTHDAY?

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,500
SOAP. YOU THINK I CAN'T RINSE A POT?

9
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,400
EVERY DINNER SINCE CHRISTMAS. WE'VE ALL NOTICED.

10
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,100
ALL OF YOU?

11
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,900
TASTE BUDS GO AS YOU GET OLDER.

12
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:34,800
BUT IF YOU CAN'T TASTE SOAP, WHAT HAPPENS WHEN YOU CAN'T SMELL GAS?

13
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,400
I'VE COOKED IN THIS KITCHEN FOR FORTY-TWO YEARS.

14
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,800
I KNOW. THAT'S WHY I DON'T WANT YOU IN IT ALONE.

15
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,400
WRENFIELD HAS A UNIT OPENING THIS MONTH. I PUT DOWN A DEPOSIT.

16
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,200
YOU ALREADY PAID?

17
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,200
NO, SHE WON'T FIGHT IT. SHE'S — SLIPPING.

18
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,900
GRANDMA, IT'S STILL THERE.

19
00:00:56,900 --> 00:01:01,000
I SCRUBBED THAT PAN THREE TIMES. NEW SOAP. NEW SPONGE.

20
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,500
AND I CAN'T TASTE A THING.

21
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,900
JADA, AM I LOSING IT?

22
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,300
I LOVE YOU, GRANDMA.

23
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,900
WASN'T SHE THE ONE PUSHING YOU INTO WRENFIELD?

24
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,200
SHE SURE WAS.

25
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,200
NOW SHE'S HERE EVERY SUNDAY, TAKING PLATES HOME. WHAT CHANGED?

26
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,500
SHE TOLD ME MY COOKING TASTED LIKE SOAP.

27
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,900
MINE TOO.

28
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,700
SHOW ME YOUR KITCHEN.

29
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,400
WHEN'D YOU BUY THESE?

30
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:34,400
AFTER THANKSGIVING. TERRANCE SENT ME AN ARTICLE ABOUT BLACK PLASTIC.

31
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,900
AND WHEN DID THE SOAP START?

32
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:39,200
CHRISTMAS.

33
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,400
SMELL IT.

34
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,200
THAT'S MY DISH SOAP.

35
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:45,000
IT SOAKS UP WHATEVER SOAP YOU USE.

36
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,200
THE MINUTE IT GETS HOT, OUT IT COMES.

37
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:50,300
BUT I CAN'T TASTE IT.

38
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:53,900
NEITHER COULD I. COOK'S ALWAYS THE LAST TO NOTICE.

39
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:58,100
THEY TESTED SILICONE BAKING PANS. IN THE OVEN, CHEMICALS LEACHED OUT.

40
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:01,400
SOME OF THEM ARE LINKED TO HORMONE DISRUPTION.

41
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:06,400
I THREW ALL MINE OUT AND GOT THESE.

42
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:09,600
WOOD? THE CHEAP ONES BLEED IN THE POT.

43
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,000
THAT'S THE FINISH, NOT THE WOOD.

44
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,700
EVERY PIECE IS ONE BLOCK OF WOOD. NO GLUE. NOTHING PAINTED ON.

45
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:20,300
THEY'RE CALLED ACAWOOD. I JUST TEXTED YOU THE LINK.

46
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:24,900
KEEP THESE TILL YOURS COME.

47
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,300
MOVERS COME SATURDAY AT NINE, MAMA.

48
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,600
SMELL THIS FIRST.

49
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:31,200
MAMA. THIS ISN'T ABOUT A SPATULA.

50
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,600
SMELL IT, TERRANCE.

51
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,200
THAT'S DISH SOAP.

52
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:38,500
NOW DOROTHY'S. SHE COOKS WITH IT EVERY DAY.

53
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,700
NOTHING.

54
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:42,200
ONE SNIFF. MY NOSE IS FINE.

55
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,400
YOU'RE THE ONE WHO SENT ME THAT ARTICLE.

56
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,000
SMELLING'S ONE THING, MAMA. TASTING'S ANOTHER.

57
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,600
FRIDAY NIGHT, I'M MAKING MY POTATO SALAD. EVERYBODY COMES.

58
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:57,300
IF ANYBODY TASTES SOAP, I'LL GET IN YOUR CAR SATURDAY AND NEVER SAY A WORD.

59
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:58,600
DEAL.

60
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:03,500
JADA. YOU FIRST. YOU'RE THE HONEST ONE.

61
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,600
GRANDMA.

62
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,500
THERE'S NO SOAP. NONE.

63
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,100
MAMA. I'M SO SORRY.

64
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:15,500
UNPACK MY BOWLS, TERRANCE.

65
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,600
SECONDS?

66
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:23,100
MY SON ALMOST MOVED ME OUT OF MY OWN KITCHEN. OVER THIS.

67
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:27,300
BEFORE ANYBODY TELLS YOU YOU'VE LOST YOUR TOUCH, SMELL YOUR SPATULA.

68
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:31,200
IF IT SMELLS LIKE DISH SOAP, SO DOES YOUR DINNER.

69
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:36,900
AND IF IT'S YOUR WIFE'S COOKING, OR YOUR MAMA'S? SMELL HERS BEFORE YOU BLAME HER.

70
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:42,600
MINE ARE ACAWOOD NOW. SEVEN PIECES, EACH ONE CUT FROM A SINGLE BLOCK OF WOOD.

71
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:48,100
NOTHING ON THEM BUT OIL OR WAX. HERE'S ONE IN HOT WATER. STILL CLEAR.

72
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,800
HAND WASH, DRY, DONE.

73
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:56,300
EIGHTY-NINE NINETY-FIVE WITH THE HOLDER. FREE SHIPPING IN THE U.S., AND NINETY-DAY RETURNS.

74
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:00,200
THE LINK'S RIGHT BELOW. AND MY KITCHEN? STILL MINE.

